# Approved requirements and integration contract

Chinese app: 110 实验室考核系统. Independent application alongside existing teaching service. Mature Vue 3+TypeScript+Vite+Naive UI+lucide-vue-next frontend; Express 5+TypeScript+pg+zod+nodemailer backend, PostgreSQL. Modern minimal ivory/slate/blue interface, left nav first item 招新考核. Responsive. No domain initially; IP test deployment, optional IP TLS. Parent owns root package.json, dependency install, deployment. server agent owns server/ except mcp.ts. client agent owns client/. MCP agent owns context-bridge/ and server/src/mcp.ts. All read shared contract. Do not modify peers' files; use notes to request interfaces.

## Current material upload contract

The user's 2026-09-28 direct-upload requirements in [DIRECT-UPLOAD.md](DIRECT-UPLOAD.md) supersede the original approval/preview/redaction/size workflow below. Active remote tools are exam_status/test_connection/submit_materials; no per-upload website approval or model review of file bodies. Original project files upload unchanged through scoped resumable HTTP tickets, maximum1GiB aggregate. One-time explicit direct-upload consent is recorded separately for existing candidates. Keep original finalization, ownership, repository binding and deadline rules. Older v1 payload/approval records and service functions remain only for stored-data compatibility and regression tests, not the current recommended flow.

## Rules
Only CQUPT students. Email verification; name, studentNo, college, major, phone, email, password. Unique email and studentNo per account. Login by email/studentNo + password. Admin email/password bootstrap via environment; never hardcode credentials. Email reset password. Roles CANDIDATE, ADMIN (reviewer role optional later; admin manages reviewers by assigning names if needed, don't fake access control).
Multiple recruitment rounds (round), batches belong to round. UNIQUE(user_id,round_id) enrollment: each user chooses ONE batch and ONE direction per round. Directions PRODUCT and DEVELOPMENT_TEST only, prestart editable, locked once started. Rejoin next round allowed. No difficulty balancing. At start, choose a published question from the same batch/direction with the fewest started participants; break ties using cryptographic randomness. Count enrollments across all versions of each question, including finalized and expired attempts, excluding unstarted or deleted enrollments. The transaction holds the batch row lock before counting and assigning, so concurrent starts see committed allocations and cannot all select the same stale minimum. New unused questions receive priority until counts catch up; existing assignments never change. Question version snapshot + attachment references lock at start. Empty pool fails without starting. Don't expose question title/content/attachments before start; rules/direction counts only.
Candidate preflight: read concrete consent policy, explicit checkbox version assessment-consent-v1; test own MCP connection before starting. Consent covers ONLY this exam project's authorized conversation files, project/user collaboration summaries, reported client/model parameters; excludes other projects, unrelated chats, credentials, hidden system/developer prompts. No covert prompt instructions. Model info can be UNKNOWN with reason, don't fabricate. Agent locates local files in approved roots, previews/redacts locally and obtains browser confirmation before sending contents. Existing files are never modified. No background wholesale history crawl.
Batch-configured 24/48h server-authoritative started_at/deadline. Snapshot duration_hours at start; existing deadlines never change when batch duration changes. opens_at <= start time < start_closes_at only gates NEW starts. After starting, all writes, MCP/OAuth and uploads depend on the personal deadline and finalization, irrespective of batch closure. OPEN future batches allow enrollment and preparation before opens_at. start is atomic/idempotent row lock; multi-tab and reload cannot restart/reroll. Countdown serverNow offset. Both repository and MCP submissions required, matching same repo SHA/version. Candidate explicitly clicks 确认交卷; after finalization no changes, even before deadline. At deadline no further writes, existing unfinalized materials retained and labeled 已截止·未交卷 (not auto-finished). Admin extension with reason/audit allowed for unfinalized attempt, not silently reset. No interview or difficulty fairness features.
Repository preview: HTTPS GitHub/Gitee only, safe provider APIs, reject URL credentials/IP/custom hosts/unsafe paths and redirects; don't execute/clone candidate code. Retrieve default/requested branch HEAD metadata. Store preview opaque id bound to user/attempt + SHA, branch, message, author, committedAt, expiry10min. Confirmation locks THAT preview SHA (not refetch latest). Before deadline allow new repo revision; invalidate/require rebind/reupload MCP when SHA changes. Final confirmation dialog shows exact SHA and MCP receipt. Providers inaccessible => clear error; no fake success.
MCP data: declared client/model metadata (reported/detected/unknown), concise project/collaboration summaries, and the current client current conversation native raw logs. Recorded direct-upload consent plus a submission request permits direct upload with notice, without another approval. No conversion, filtering, trimming or reconstruction; bytes stay outside model/MCP argument context. At most20 files/1GiB via scoped resumable HTTP tickets; helper/bridge snapshots handle append-only growth. Missing native logs or permissions are real blockers, not reasons to substitute other sessions. Repository binding, deadline, token ownership and explicit website finalization remain enforced. Only admin can read/download received material; candidates see progress and receipts. Retain90days after result release (or deadline if unpublished), then purge content with audit. Legacy v1 stored payload/approvals remain compatible for historical data only. Never log bodies or tokens.
Admin: rounds and batches CRUD/time scheduling, question editing/publishing with attachments (upload), candidate list/filter, details with repository locked SHA and MCP materials, scoring/feedback, publish results+email notification, CSV export safe formula escaping, audit records. Attachment private authenticated downloads only after start, safe filename/content-type, 20MB limit, admin uploads. Assessment data persists PostgreSQL plus owned uploads volume. Result unpublished invisible candidate. No server execution of repo code.

## API wire convention
Base /api, JSON. Success returns data object directly, errors {message,code?}, HTTP status meaningful. UUID ids. camelCase JSON. ISO timestamps. Cookies HttpOnly session, SameSite=Lax/Strict; CSRF token from GET /api/auth/me and header X-CSRF-Token required for authenticated mutating browser requests. Verify Origin against APP_ORIGIN for cookie writes; MCP bearer routes separately scoped. All DB SQL parametrized; locks/transactions for start/confirm/finalize. Login/register/send-code throttled by DB/IP+subject; passwords scrypt (node crypto) or argon2. No unverified emails, no code in response/log. SMTP outbox durable retry. Test mail transport ONLY explicit nonproduction config.

GET /api/health -> {status:'ok',database:'ok'}
POST /api/auth/email-code {email,purpose:'REGISTER'|'RESET'} -> {challengeId,expiresIn:600}
POST /api/auth/register {name,studentNo,college,major,phone,email,password,challengeId,code,acceptedPolicy:true} -> {user,csrfToken}
POST /api/auth/login {account,password} -> {user,csrfToken}
GET /api/auth/me -> {user,csrfToken} or401
POST /api/auth/logout -> {ok:true}
POST /api/auth/reset-password {email,challengeId,code,password} -> {ok:true}
User {id,role,name,studentNo?,college?,major?,phone?,email}
GET /api/batches -> {rounds:[{id,name,batches:[{id,name,description,status:'DRAFT'|'OPEN'|'CLOSED',opensAt,startClosesAt,durationHours:24|48,directions:['PRODUCT','DEVELOPMENT_TEST'],enrollment?}]}],serverNow}
POST /api/enrollments {batchId,direction} -> {enrollment}
PATCH /api/enrollments/:id {batchId?,direction} -> {enrollment}
GET /api/enrollments/:id -> {enrollment,serverNow}
Enrollment {id,roundId,batchId,batchName,roundName,direction,state:'READY'|'ACTIVE'|'FINALIZED'|'EXPIRED',mcpConnected:boolean,consentAccepted:boolean,startedAt:null|ISO,deadline:null|ISO,finalizedAt:null|ISO,question:null|{title,content,attachments:[{id,name,size,url}]},repository:null|{id,url,branch,sha,message,author,committedAt,confirmedAt},materials:null|{id,sha256,repoSha,receivedAt,clientCount,fileCount,coverage},approvals:[{id,manifest,payloadHash,repoSha,state,expiresAt}],result:null|{score,feedback,publishedAt}}
POST /api/enrollments/:id/consent {version:'assessment-consent-v1',accepted:true} -> {enrollment}
POST /api/enrollments/:id/mcp-token {} -> {token,mcpUrl,expiresAt}; rotate explicit; token only returned once; revoke prior tokens. MCP URL /mcp. Tokens valid for own enrollment preflight then until deadline/finalization.
POST /api/enrollments/:id/start {confirmed:true,expectedDurationHours:24|48} -> {enrollment,serverNow}; require consent+mcpConnected; changed duration requires 409 DURATION_CHANGED and explicit reconfirmation.
POST /api/enrollments/:id/repository/preview {url,branch?} -> {preview:{id,url,branch,sha,message,author,committedAt,expiresAt}}
POST /api/enrollments/:id/repository/confirm {previewId} -> {enrollment}
POST /api/enrollments/:id/approvals/:approvalId/approve {approved:true} -> {ok:true}
GET /api/enrollments/:id/materials -> {payload,receipt} (admin only; candidates including owner receive 403; after content purge return metadata+purged)
POST /api/enrollments/:id/finalize {repositoryId,materialsId,confirmed:true} -> {enrollment,receipt:{id,submittedAt,sha,materialsHash}}
GET /api/attachments/:id -> authenticated file; associated own question already started orADMIN
GET /api/admin/overview -> {counts:{candidates,batches,active,finalized,unreviewed},recent:[]}
GET/POST /api/admin/rounds -> {rounds:[{id,name}]} / {round}; body{name}
GET /api/admin/batches -> {batches:[{id,roundId,roundName,name,description,opensAt,startClosesAt,durationHours,status:'DRAFT'|'OPEN'|'CLOSED'}]}
POST /api/admin/batches; PATCH /api/admin/batches/:id {roundId,name,description,opensAt,startClosesAt,durationHours:24|48,status}
GET /api/admin/questions?batchId= -> {questions:[{id,batchId,direction,title,content,published,attachments:[]}]}
POST /api/admin/questions; PATCH /api/admin/questions/:id {batchId,direction,title,content,published,attachmentIds:[]}
POST /api/admin/attachments (multipart file) -> {attachment:{id,name,size,url}}
GET /api/admin/candidates?search=&state=&batchId= -> {candidates:[{...user,enrollments:[{...Enrollment}]}]} (paginate ifneeded stable limit100)
GET /api/admin/enrollments/:id -> {enrollment,user,review:{score,feedback,publishedAt}|null}
POST /api/admin/enrollments/:id/extend {minutes,reason} -> {enrollment}
POST /api/admin/enrollments/:id/review {score:0..100,feedback} -> {review}; only finalized
POST /api/admin/enrollments/:id/publish {} -> {review}; releases result/email via outbox idempotent
GET /api/admin/export -> CSV
GET /api/admin/audit -> {events:[{id,actorName,action,createdAt,details}]} (redacted no conversation/rawtoken)

## Backend/MCP integration boundary (must match exports)
server agent creates server/src/context.ts exports:
- type AppContext { pool:pg.Pool; config:{appOrigin:string; storageDir:string; ...}; ... }
- createContext() -> Promise<AppContext>
server/src/app.ts exports createApp(ctx:AppContext) -> Express application, mounts registerMcp(app,ctx) imported './mcp.js'. During development missing mcp file parent supplies placeholder once.
server/src/assessment.ts exports function authenticateMcp(ctx:AppContext,rawToken:string):Promise<{userId:string,enrollmentId:string}>; getMcpStatus(ctx,identity):Promise<{enrollment:Enrollment,serverNow:string}>; probeMcp(ctx,identity):Promise<{ok:true,...}>; prepareMcpMaterials(ctx,identity,input:{manifest:MaterialManifest,payloadHash:string,repoSha:string}):Promise<{approvalId,approvalUrl,expiresAt}>; submitMcpMaterials(ctx,identity,input:{approvalId:string,payload:MaterialPayload}):Promise<{receipt:{id,sha256,repoSha,receivedAt},status:string}>.
Manifest {files:[{name:string,sha256:string,bytes:number,source:string,coverage:'export'|'partial'}],clients:[{name:string,version?:string,models:[{name:string,parameters?:Record<string,string|number|boolean|null>,source:'reported'|'detected'|'unknown'}]}],projectSummary:string,collaborationSummary:string}
Payload {schemaVersion:1,repoSha:string,manifest:MaterialManifest,files:[{name:string,content:string}]}. sha256 is canonicalJSON recursively lexicographically sorted object keys, arrayorder preserved, UTF8. Backend should export canonicalJson from server/src/security.ts; bridge independently samealgorithm tests. File sha256 hashes UTF8 content; sum bytes max10MB; no duplicate/pathlike names; payload summary<=20000 chars; files20 each<=1MB. Servers validate structure, SHA, exact manifest content match signed approval, reject obvious secret markers e.g PRIVATE KEY, sk-/ghp_/AKIA credential patterns while avoiding false detection of normal prose. Browser approve shows manifest summaries+filenames+coverage, not raw absolute local paths. All auth/deadline/final/idempotency enforcement implemented in assessment.ts by server agent.
MCP agent only uses exported business services, never direct SQL/schema modification. Remote StreamableHTTP tools: exam_status, test_connection, submit_materials. Local stdio bridge: exam_status, test_connection, find_candidate_files, submit_files. No per-upload approval tool and no finalization tool. Discovery is metadata-only inside explicit authorized roots; workspace matching is not current-conversation identity. Use current session id/path/index metadata to select native logs. Raw bytes are copied/hashed/transferred by code. Startup/connection never initiates upload. See DIRECT-UPLOAD.md for current behavior. STDIO stdout remains protocol-only, with redacted diagnostic errors on stderr.

## Acceptance
Auth validation/expiry/one-time codes/rate limits; concurrent start onequestiononeclock; secrets/content inaccessible prestart/crossuser; expiry and multi-tab locks; one enrollment perround; questionversions immutable; repo preview locks displayed SHA and update invalidates MCP; MCP token scope, consent, websiteapproval required, payload/hash checks and idempotency; double finalize stable receipt; result privacy; CSV injection; context scanner authorizedroots/no symlink escapes/no bulkhistory/nosecrets; real API+MCP protocol tests and frontend built typechecked. Keep testcase-only adapters excluded in production. Parent integrates Docker+SMTP+realpublicrepository+browser tests before deployment.

## 注册保护接口补充

发注册验证码前，浏览器使用 GET `/api/auth/registration-challenge?email=...` 获取绑定邮箱与签名浏览器 Cookie 的 ALTCHA 挑战。POST `/api/auth/email-code` 在 purpose=REGISTER 时必须携带 `registrationProof`；RESET 不需要此字段。成功验证与邮件入队在同一事务中一次性完成。验证码成功校验后才进行密码哈希。

运营通过 GET `/api/admin/registration-risk?ids=...` 读取当前候选人的核查信息，PATCH `/api/admin/candidates/:id/registration-risk` 使用 `RESTRICT_START`、`ALLOW_START` 或 `CLEAR_FLAG` 并填写 reason。所有操作需要管理员身份及 CSRF 令牌。注册保护额度和升级说明见 REGISTRATION-AND-TIMING.md。
